# Zero-Mem Obsidian projection — OPERATOR configuration example.
#
# Copy to `config/projection.yaml` and set your own vault path. This file is an
# EXAMPLE only: it is never read by the product, and `config/projection.yaml` is
# optional — absent is the normal state.
#
# The vault root is runtime/operator configuration. It is deliberately NOT a
# product constant: no username, home directory, or `~/Obsidian` guess appears
# anywhere in `src/projection/`.
#
# Resolution order (plan-m9.md §2.2), highest precedence first:
#   1. explicit argument   -> ProjectionConfig(vault_root=...) / load_projection_config(...)
#   2. environment         -> ZERO_MEM_OBSIDIAN_VAULT=/absolute/path/to/YourVault
#   3. this file           -> vault_root below
#   4. nothing configured  -> projection is UNAVAILABLE and writes nothing, anywhere
#
# Requirements for `vault_root`: absolute, existing, a directory, not a symlink,
# writable, not your home directory, not the repository root, not an `.obsidian`
# directory. A `~` form is rejected: it is a guess, not an explicit path.
#
# Zero-Mem owns ONLY the dedicated subtree `<vault_root>/Zero-Mem/`. The vault
# root itself, `.obsidian/`, and all your other notes are never written to.

vault_root: /absolute/path/to/YourObsidianVault
